From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:19:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: retain numeric SOCKS5 method codes and padded hex
 diagnostics

Convert the wrong-authentication-method error, preserving non-dropping
Error, its complete lowercase %02x message and false return. The actual
uint8 method fits the existing int64 ErrorCode key exactly. No new fields,
renderer behavior, destination, credentials or negotiation changes.

Add a public Socks5 test with scripted Send/Recv on an explicitly invalid
base descriptor. Values 0x0a and 0xff verify zero padding/full byte values,
the rejection result and exactly one method request/response. No socket is
opened, no network traffic occurs and auth=null avoids credential handling.

Shared eCash netbase owner. Source-only event lint/diff checks pass; new
native case NOT_COMPILED/NOT_RUN. The separate pre-existing credential debug
site is unchanged and reported to the coordinator; it is not exempted or
silently folded into this mechanical conversion. Sealed381 unchanged.

Scripted production diff:
/private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/convert.py --root . --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/socks5-auth-method-diagnostic.json --report /Users/shammah/repos/lotus-v2-repair-work/logging-cleanup/socks414-conversion.json --apply
git clang-format --force --binary /opt/homebrew/bin/clang-format --style '{BasedOnStyle: InheritParentConfig, BreakStringLiterals: false}' HEAD -- src/netbase.cpp src/test/netbase_tests.cpp

